    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Four-week COPD review after starting tiotropium-olodaterol. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Nimoy returns four weeks after starting tiotropium-olodaterol two inhalations each morning. He feels a little less tight in the chest in the mornings and has cut his albuterol from once or twice a day to about four times a week. He still has to stop for breath after about 100 meters on level ground. The dose counter shows no missed doses. He has had no flare-up, increase in sputum, fever, or need for antibiotics or prednisone. He has no dry mouth, difficulty passing urine, palpitations, or tremor. He saw the pulmonologist this morning, and his 6-minute walk test was done in the pulmonary function laboratory. He starts pulmonary rehabilitation next week. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Mornings easier; still stops after about 100 meters</td></tr><tr><td>Reliever use</td><td>Albuterol about four times a week, down from once or twice a day</td></tr><tr><td>Adherence</td><td>No missed doses by dose counter</td></tr><tr><td>Exacerbations</td><td>None since intake, and none in the past 12 months</td></tr><tr><td>Medication tolerance</td><td>No dry mouth, urinary difficulty, palpitations, or tremor</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Positive</td><td>Breathless on walking about 100 meters or one flight of stairs; little cough; small amount of clear morning sputum</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Negative</td><td>No chest pain, palpitations, orthopnea, or ankle swelling</td></tr><tr><td>Genitourinary</td><td>Negative</td><td>No hesitancy or retention</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Negative</td><td>Mood steady; no panic with breathlessness</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

